   "start": 0.32,
   "text": "Even the villi move. They shorten quickly, lengthen slowly, and sway from side to side. Local reflexes trigger this when chyme touches them, and so does villikinin, a hormone released when digestive products contact the mucosa. Each squeeze helps absorption and pumps lymph out of the central lacteal."
